[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_lndbs")
dialogue_id = "debate_collision"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Shard Collisions"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: The Scribe tells us that when the Enlightened One's Abode joined with its neighbor shard, it was a divine sign.
historian: But it isn't the first time that has happened.
historian: I have here a report from the Explorer, describing a massive shard that used to be three separate landmasses, a fact widely known by its inhabitants.
historian: These landmasses drifted together centuries ago and none of us knew about it.
historian: It turns out that when ten thousand islands drift in the Cloud Sea, sometimes they bump into each other.
historian: We are so desperate for a grand narrative to make sense of our shattered world, that we look at natural coincidences and call them destiny.
historian: If two leaves floating down a stream stick together, we don't see a divine plan, but when the same happens on a larger scale, we attribute meaning to the event.
historian: It is a dangerous thing to base the future of our civilization on a coincidence."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
